<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Each sentence describes a rule or a fact. Choose the sign that makes the statement below it true.</p><ol><li><p>A water tank on a roof in Machakos cannot hold more than 2000 litres. It holds <m>v</m> litres.</p><div><m>{v}</m> [ &lt; | ≤ | &gt; | ≥ ] <m>{2000}</m>  </div></li><li><p>The temperature in Lodwar was above <m>35\,^\circ\text{C}</m> all afternoon. The temperature was <m>t\,^\circ\text{C}</m>.</p><div><m>{t}</m> [ &lt; | ≤ | &gt; | ≥ ] <m>{35}</m>  </div></li><li><p>Fewer than 40 matatus left the stage before 6 am. The number was <m>m</m>.</p><div><m>{m}</m> [ &lt; | ≤ | &gt; | ≥ ] <m>{40}</m>  </div></li><li><p>A plot must have an area of at least 450 square metres before a house is built on it. A plot of <m>k</m> square metres is big enough.</p><div><m>{k}</m> [ &lt; | ≤ | &gt; | ≥ ] <m>{450}</m>  </div></li></ol></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Find the key words, then ask two questions: is the letter bigger or smaller than the number, and is the number itself allowed?</p><ol><li><p>The key words are <em>cannot hold more than</em>, so <m>{v}</m> is at most <m>{2000}</m>: <m>{v}</m> <m>\le</m> <m>{2000}</m>. The number <m>{2000}</m> itself is allowed: a filled circle at <m>{2000}</m> on a number line, with everything to the left.</p></li><li><p>The key words are <em>above</em>, so <m>{t}</m> is more than <m>{35}</m>: <m>{t}</m> <m>\gt</m> <m>{35}</m>. The number <m>{35}</m> itself is not allowed: an open circle at <m>{35}</m> on a number line, with everything to the right.</p></li><li><p>The key words are <em>fewer than</em>, so <m>{m}</m> is less than <m>{40}</m>: <m>{m}</m> <m>\lt</m> <m>{40}</m>. The number <m>{40}</m> itself is not allowed: an open circle at <m>{40}</m> on a number line, with everything to the left.</p></li><li><p>The key words are <em>at least</em>, so <m>{k}</m> is at least <m>{450}</m>: <m>{k}</m> <m>\ge</m> <m>{450}</m>. The number <m>{450}</m> itself is allowed: a filled circle at <m>{450}</m> on a number line, with everything to the right.</p></li></ol></p></solution>
    <answer><p>≤</p></answer>
    <answer><p>&gt;</p></answer>
    <answer><p>&lt;</p></answer>
    <answer><p>≥</p></answer>
</stack-static>